# Docker build context exclusions for both deploy/Dockerfile.api and deploy/Dockerfile.web.
#
# Two goals: keep the build context small, and make it structurally impossible for a local .env
# file or a build artifact from a developer's machine to end up inside an image layer.

.git
.github

**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.turbo

# Real env files are never part of the build context. Only committed .env.example templates
# (which contain no values) are allowed through.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Editor/OS noise
.vscode
.idea
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# This deploy scaffolding itself is not part of any image's build context.
deploy/**/*.env
